          "title": "In memory of Freland Johnson 07/05/1954 to 02/27/2025",
          "meta": "07/05/4 to 02/27/2025",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "header3",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3",
          "_anchor": "header3-ca"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": "2",
            "paddingBottom": "2",
            "bgColor": "#fff"
          },
          "text": "<p>In memory of Freland Johnson 07/05/1954 to 02/27/2025\r</p><p>Today we celebrate the Life of Captain Freland Johnson. He passed away February 27th at his home in Heron Bay with his family by his side.\r</p><p><br></p><p>Captain Freland is preceded in death by his father Samuel F Johnson; his mother Ova Johnson; His brother Marel Johnson; His sons Jason Hill &amp; Baby Freland A Johnson Jr; His grandson Jonas Freland lyons.\r</p><p><br></p><p>He is survived by his wife Pam; His children Lee, Brandis, Krystal &amp; Scott; His brother Leo (Linda); His sisters Callie (Neil) &amp; Annette (John-Dee); His sister-in-law Dana Johnson; His grandchildren Jesse, Shaun, Caleb, Bryahna, Asher &amp; Autumn; As well as nieces &amp; nephews, other relatives, many friends &amp; his legion family.\r</p><p><br></p><p>A celebration of life will be held on March 22, 2025\r</p><p>from 12-2 at the American legion Post 250\r</p><p>in the Bayley Hall in Fowl River.</p><p>\r</p><p>\r</p><p>\r</p><p>\r</p><p>\n</p><p>\n</p><p>\n</p><p>\n</p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_sourceTheme": "mobirise3",
          "_anchor": "content1-cc",
          "_styles": {
            "P": {
